        <text type="fire_danger_footer">
          <p>Notes</p>
          <p>Fire Danger Ratings are routinely issued by 5 pm daily during the fire season. Always ensure you have the latest forecast.</p>
          <p>Fire Danger Ratings are determined in conjunction with the Country Fire Service (CFS).</p>
          <p>For information on Total Fire Bans and how to prepare for fires, visit the CFS web page at www.cfs.sa.gov.au or call the CFS Bushfire Information Hotline on 1800 362 361</p>
          <p>For all weather information, visit the Bureau of Meteorology web page at www.bom.gov.au.</p>
          <p>Note: On occasion Fire Danger Ratings may not adhere to FBI thresholds and issued FDR values below due to bushfire control agency discretion.</p>
          <p>Produced by SACFS GIS.</p>
        </text>
